{"id": 39, "ts": 1781173182.4285371, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s thorough recap of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s record. The recent clarification from Sarah that we have no concrete examples of Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision\u2011making quality under pressure weakens the case for B, especially given the importance of proven judgment in high\u2011risk, long\u2011distance flights. While B does handle stress well and assesses weather effectively, the lack of documented decision outcomes, combined with the noted weak numeric memory and his tendency to make nasty remarks toward colleagues, raises concerns about both attention to detail and crew cooperation.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC brings documented 100\u202f% reliability, a consistently positive crew atmosphere, and demonstrated ability to make correct decisions quickly and stay calm in crises. Although his communication style is challenging, there is no evidence that this has led to safety\u2011critical failures, and his technical competence is solid.\nGiven the current evidence, I am shifting my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**. I believe his proven reliability and decision quality outweigh the communication shortcomings, especially when compared to the uncertainties surrounding Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision\u2011making record and interpersonal behavior."}
